      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We use the distributive law to multiply each term in the first expression by each term in the second expression, obtaining \\begin{align*}\n&2x(x+5) + 3(x+5) \\quad \\text{distributing the} \\ \\\\ &2x \\quad \\text{and } 3 \n+ 2x \\cdot 5 + 3 \\cdot 5 \\quad \\text{distributing the last} \\ \\\\ &2x + 3 \\quad \\text{and } 5 \\ \\\\ &=2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15 \n+ 10x + 15 \\quad \\text{combining the first} \\\\ &2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 30x + 15 + 15 \\quad \\text{combining again} \n= &2x^2 + 53x + 30 \\quad \\text{final expression}.\\end{align*}\nThe statement \"$2x^2+53x+30$\" is equal to our final expression. So, we can write, \\[\\boxed{2x^2+53x+30}=\\boxed{(2x+3)(x+5)}.\\] The answer is 2x^2+53x+30",
